###* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|page=472|passage=She leads him towards the steps, drawing him by the odour of her armpits, the vice of her painted eyes, the rustle of her slip in whose sinuous folds lurks the lion reek of all the male brutes that have '''possessed''' her.}}
###* {{quote-book|en|year=1953|year_published=1955|author=w:Ian Fleming|title={{w|Casino Royale (novel)|Casino Royale}}|volume=|location=London|publisher=Pan Books|chapter=Tide of Passion|page=167|passage=She would surrender herself avidly, he thought, and greedily enjoy all the intimacies of the bed without ever allowing herself to be '''possessed'''.}}
